The objective of this task was to create a script that validates email formats using Regular Expressions (Regex).

Validation Logic: The script uses grep -E with a regex pattern ^[a-zA-Z0-9]+@[a-zA-Z]+\.com$ to identify standard email structures.

Processing:
Valid emails are sorted and filtered for uniqueness (uniq) before being saved to valid.txt.
Invalid emails (those not matching the pattern) are captured using the invert-match flag -v and saved to invalid.txt.
